  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Support Centre</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mondiaal FNV and the FNV trade union increasingly act as technical partners. For example, Mondiaal FNV has an active advisory role in financial sustainability. Partners also specifically requested technical support and consultancy in negotiating and collective bargaining in organising, lobbying and campaigning. Mondiaal FNV intermediated and pinpointed the right FNV colleagues. In this context, Mondiaal FNV also cooperates closely with the Dutch Employers Cooperation Programme (DECP) in supporting social dialogue processes (the &#x2018;Harvard&#x2019; methodology) and offered apprenticeships and study visits to the Netherlands. Strengthening financial management in partner organisations is also covered in this activity.
In the coming years, direct technical cooperation, in addition to financial support, will expand because of the growing demand from our partners. Mondiaal FNV will mobilise technical support and expertise, on a demand basis, offering training programmes, coaching, mediation, exchange visits, apprenticeships and scholarships. We will organise this in a &#x2018;Technical Support Centre&#x2019;. The Centre will also include matching with experts from other countries and organisations, where they are better equipped. For social dialogue, Mondiaal FNV will work in close cooperation with DECP to provide sound support. Partners can apply for technical support and include it in the projects and programmes. In countries where the TUCP programme is phasing out or has already been concluded, partners/former partners may apply for concrete technical support as part of their exit strategy. 
Specific technical expertise can also be provided at the request of other organisations such as Dutch companies, NGOs and embassies, if short-term interventions can be successful without developing a long-standing relationship.</narrative>
  </description>
